# Writing documentation

Four linters guard the text in this repository. One command runs them all, and it is part
of CI:

```bash
vp run lint:docs   # markdownlint-cli2 + textlint + cspell + secretlint (~10s)
vp run fix:docs    # the autofixable half of markdownlint and textlint
vp run lint:links  # dead / redirected links — network, so it is not in lint:docs
```

| Tool | Owns | Config |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [markdownlint-cli2](https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint-cli2) | Markdown structure: headings, lists, fenced-code languages, table alignment | `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` |
| [textlint](https://github.com/textlint/textlint) + `terminology` | how product names and technical terms are written | `.textlintrc.json` |
| [cspell](https://github.com/streetsidesoftware/cspell) | spelling, in prose **and** in source comments and identifiers | `cspell.json` |
| [secretlint](https://github.com/secretlint/secretlint) | credentials committed by accident | `.secretlintrc.json` |

## When a linter fires

- **cspell flags a word** — add it to `.cspell/project-words.txt` only when it is a real
  name, API or term of art (`prefault`, `stringbool`, `metavar`); lowercase, in the
  section it belongs to. When it is an ordinary word, cspell is right: fix the text.
  British and American spellings are both accepted (`"language": "en,en-GB"`).
- **textlint flags a term** — write the product name the way its owners write it:
  **ArkType**, **TypeBox**, **Valibot**, **Zod**, **Effect Schema**, **JSON Schema**,
  **OpenAPI**. `readme` and `regex` are deliberately exempt from the default list.
- **markdownlint flags a table** (`MD060`) — the tables here are padded to align, so
  changing the width of one cell means re-padding that column in every row of the table.
  Line length (`MD013`) is off: wrap prose where it reads well.
- **A link redirects** — fix the target rather than following the redirect. That check is
  what caught the README pointing at Effect Schema's v3 docs while the generator emits the
  v4 API, so run `vp run lint:links` after touching any link.

Suppress a rule only in the rare case where it is wrong, at the line it fires on
(`<!-- textlint-disable -->`, `<!-- cspell:disable-next-line -->`), never by loosening the
config for the whole repository.
